  "text_input": "Patient presented with yellowish discoloration of eyes for 20 days, abdominal distension for 15 days, and bilateral lower limb swelling for 5 days. He reported passing high-colored urine. No history of fever, abdominal pain, hematemesis, or melena. Past history includes alcohol consumption for 25 years (daily drinker). Examination revealed icterus and gross ascites. USG showed hepatomegaly with coarse echotexture, surface nodularity, splenomegaly, and gross ascites, suggestive of chronic liver parenchymal disease. 2D Echo was normal. Diagnosed with decompensated chronic liver parenchymal disease with portal hypertension, grade 2 esophageal varices (Child-Pugh Class C, MELD-31), grade 2 internal hemorrhoids, and type 2 diabetes mellitus.",
